#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565535} :activity/id #uuid "7731ce61-1f9a-51e4-a49c-996258564f67" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049027 :topic/id #uuid "d4a5e636-5453-5120-957b-34a9e32197ae" :topic/math-academy-id 1403} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565501 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565454 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03661a97-3f4c-57e9-943b-6740f23533e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{67}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564944} {:answer/id #uuid "24b2b15c-24e2-57bc-9b13-a06cbd4eb16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{69}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564994} {:answer/id #uuid "7335ea22-0c13-5b37-8b47-351229d967ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{73}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565114} {:answer/id #uuid "7c88601f-7ff0-5a6b-af0b-a77dbae473cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{72}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565128} {:answer/id #uuid "aa458a18-ad45-591e-ab81-1483b9bbc230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565192}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565192} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddd44795-8d4c-547b-9853-d23d19571f47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ae1938a1-58ee-571b-a544-d365ce409563" :question/math-academy-id "q-21232" :question/problem "![](images/19/19ca38571817d9de8c92de17d5121c33ac1494848766033792dc9586c95fa475.png)\n\nIn the isosceles triangle $△ABC$  with base $\\overset{―}{AB}$, point $E$ lies on the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$, $\\overset{―}{AE}=\\overset{―}{EC}$ and $m∠EAC={40}^{∘}.$ What is the measure of $∠B?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle with base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Consequently,  the base angles must have equal measure:\n\n$$\nm∠BAC=m∠B\n$$\n\nAlso, since $△CEA$ is an isosceles triangle, we have:\n\n$$\nm∠C=m∠EAC={40}^{∘}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $m∠B$ using the fact that the interior angles of $△ABC$ sum to ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BAC+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+m∠B+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠B & ={140}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={70}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3970f23e-0d4b-58af-b62e-7ed9157998d2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565505}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565505 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46ca1c05-5190-5ad2-8c5c-d591894996c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{107}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565039} {:answer/id #uuid "5274cb9d-d489-5332-8ddc-d0bf62c38087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{108}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565058} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa840cd-3123-510e-bf31-113dff14f21e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{112}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565228} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ebedab-b10c-56a0-8c29-72fe32d8a4eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{113}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565312} {:answer/id #uuid "f81ae10f-b2ec-5eff-a612-29b4fa814574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565315}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565315} :answer-field/id #uuid "2517a418-b87f-54f2-b710-d15c568a3534" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a323077c-5cf0-5ef0-a051-240e1171e494" :question/math-academy-id "q-52972" :question/problem "![](images/37/372ac1135e480bcd843f02b05bdeae42d462fccaced8151e4a355d6263d7be64.png)\n\nFind the value of $z$ in the triangle shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, from the diagram, notice that $∠CAB$ and $∠BAD$ are supplementary. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAB+m∠BAD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠CAB+z & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠CAB & ={180}^{∘}-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle where $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{BC}$, the base angles must be equal:\n\n$$\nm∠C=m∠CAB.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the interior angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAB+m∠C+m∠B & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠CAB+m∠B & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2({180}^{∘}-z)+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {360}^{∘}-2z+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2z & ={220}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={110}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "547a136f-0f45-5073-888d-a69eb3373469"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565535 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565459 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7af2094e-5a9c-5576-ab4c-588a0176acd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565125} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5c018b-da77-51b3-94a3-4a719e2c22a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{29}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565132} {:answer/id #uuid "8be640ca-b6bd-59dc-98b9-bc210f8e3e6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{27}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565154} {:answer/id #uuid "a51bdf43-9f1b-54de-9f2e-2698aa8af185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565189} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b5d134-db45-5c5c-a672-02898c3558d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{34}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565213}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565189} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b88805-312e-50ff-a48f-9a2d91e7b91d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b85bf70e-60cf-531c-93a8-54cd5e2b47c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-21222" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c62f51c2b029d6b1e24e7f30603c5f34ab5d70d96ed84c5c74de15d4e2e6358e.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $∠D?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $△ABC$ is an equilateral triangle. Consequently, all of the interior angles must be equal to ${60}^{∘}:$ \n\n$$\nm∠A=m∠B=m∠ABC={60}^{∘}\n$$\n\nAlso, since $△CDB$ is an isosceles triangle, the base angles must have equal measure:\n\n$$\nm∠CBD=m∠D\n$$\n\nNotice also that $∠ACB$ and $∠DCB$ are supplementary, therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ACB+m∠DCB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {60}^{∘}+m∠DCB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠DCB & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Finally, we calculate $m∠D$ using the fact that the interior angles of a triangle sum to ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠D+m∠DCB+m∠CBD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D+{120}^{∘}+m∠D & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠D & ={60}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d4131835-327a-579d-bd13-775bb94299f0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565501}}] :activity/title "The Isosceles Triangle Theorem" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564931}]}
